<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7128" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cătĭus</span></b> , ii,
			m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A Roman deity</i>, <i>the protector of
				boys</i>, <i>whom he made intelligent</i>
			(catos), Aug. Civ. Dei, 4, 21.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An Epicurean philosopher</i>, <i>author of works</i> de rerum naturā, de summo bono,
			etc., <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam. 15, 16, 1</span></i>; Cass.
					<i><span class="en">ib. 15, 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint.
				10, 1, 124</span></i>; Schol. Cruq. ad <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 2,
				4, 1</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cătĭānus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spectra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 15, 16, 1</span></i>
			; Cass. <i><span class="en">ib. 15,
			19</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A feigned name</i> in <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 2,
				4, 1</span></i> and 88. </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
